                            <comment id="16782628" author="itsick" created="Sun, 3 Mar 2019 08:04:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dmekhanikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dmekhanikov&quot;&gt;dmekhanikov&lt;/a&gt;&#160;I have couple of questions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Do you have a workaround / mitigation for this?&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Do you have an ETA for the fix?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Thanks&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16782634" author="dmekhanikov" created="Sun, 3 Mar 2019 08:40:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=itsick&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;itsick&quot;&gt;itsick&lt;/a&gt; the workaround is to use &lt;a href=&quot;https://ignite.apache.org/releases/latest/javadoc/org/apache/ignite/IgniteCache.html#clear-K-&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;IgniteCache#clear(...)&lt;/a&gt; method instead of remove. It removes the entry from cache only if no operations are performed concurrently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently nobody seems to be working on the fix, so you can take it over. At this point it&apos;s unclear, if it&apos;s possible to guarantee consistency at all, when readThrough is enabled, but writeThrough is disabled. We need to research this point first.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16795948" author="agoncharuk" created="Tue, 19 Mar 2019 10:25:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dmekhanikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dmekhanikov&quot;&gt;dmekhanikov&lt;/a&gt;, can you take a look?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16796067" author="ignitetcbot" created="Tue, 19 Mar 2019 13:09:29 +0000"  >&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #D6F7C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: All: No blockers found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=3344837&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;TeamCity &lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: All&lt;/b&gt; Results&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16796122" author="dmekhanikov" created="Tue, 19 Mar 2019 14:02:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt; the changes look good to me. Consider adding tests for transactional caches and having at least one backup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also I think, it would be good to have a test like follows, just to fix the behaviour:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
@Test
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; void testRemoveIsApplied() &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throws&lt;/span&gt; Exception {
    startGrid(0);

    IgniteEx client = startGrid(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;client&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);

    IgniteCache&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt; cache = client.cache(TEST_CACHE);

    &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt; key = &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;key&quot;&lt;/span&gt;;

    assertNotNull(cache.get(key));

    IgniteFuture&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt; getFut = cache.getAsync(key);

    cache.remove(key);

    assertNotNull(getFut.get());

    assertNull(cache.localPeek(key)); &lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;// Check, that remove actually takes place.
&lt;/span&gt;
    assertNotNull(cache.get(key));
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16796971" author="agoncharuk" created="Wed, 20 Mar 2019 09:51:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Tests were added, re-triggered test suite.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16797094" author="agoncharuk" created="Wed, 20 Mar 2019 12:00:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
